    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d394">

                <pb facs="0513" n="429" sameAs="frus:frus1903/pg429"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Tower to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Embassy of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-12-29"><hi rendition="#italic">December 29,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 10.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose to you herewith
                    a copy and a translation into English of the memorandum relating to the claims
                    of Germany against Venezuela, which accompanied the note of the German
                    Government to which my dispatch No. 6 of the 24th December has reference.</p>
                <p>I was unable to inclose this memorandum to you with that dispatch, because as the
                    mail was leaving at once there was not time enough, to my regret, to have the
                    translation finished, neither did I wish to delay my dispatch by reason of its
                    far greater importance; therefore, I sent it forward with a copy of the
                    memorandum.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charlemagne
                    Tower.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d394-a1.xml" xpointer="d394-a1"/>
            </div>
